# ls — caps.decl
#
# Format: R90-XREPO.013.M1-001 line-oriented caps.decl grammar
# (paideia-os design/architecture/caps-decl-format.md, whose own §3.3
# worked example is this tool: "ls: read files + directory entries +
# resolve schemas"). Adopted at R90-XREPO.013.M4-001 (this repo's
# issue #31), replacing the R50-vintage prose "requires:" /
# "declares_output_schemas:" declaration this file used to carry (see
# git history for the superseded freeform text). Mirrors the same
# adoption pass landed for the volume trio: mkfs.pdxfs (#23,
# b6dff27db5), mount.pdxfs (#20), umount.pdxfs (#20).
#
# `!KIND_FOO <mask>` = mandatory: exec fails -EACCES if the parent's
# cap-set does not hold at least this mask. ` KIND_FOO <mask>` (no
# `!`) = optional: narrowed to at most this mask, dropped to zero if
# the parent held none. See the format doc §3.1 / §4 for the full
# narrowing semantics. Grammar is strict: every non-comment,
# non-blank line must be a decl-line or the whole file is refused
# (§3) — the notes below stay in `#` comments for exactly that
# reason.

!KIND_USER               0x001   # invoker attribution (audit) + owner column resolution
!KIND_TTY                0x002   # write rendered output (text/--json/--color) to the invoking terminal
!KIND_PDXFS_FILE         0x001   # READ_BYTES (directory + file content read)
 KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT       0x001   # semantic-pipe stdout (--schema/--json framing), deferred

# Notes (carried forward from the R50 prose decl):
#
# - KIND_USER, KIND_TTY, and KIND_PDXFS_FILE are mandatory: ls cannot
#   attribute the audit-first invariant (D3, r49-r50-plan.md §1),
#   cannot render any output, and cannot read the target directory
#   without them respectively.
# - KIND_USER's R_USER_READ (0x001) covers both invoker attribution
#   at audit_begin (src/audit_shim.pdx) and the `-l` owner column,
#   which hand-decodes a per-entry KIND_USER wire-form cap via
#   libpdx-cap::cap_unpack (src/owner_col.pdx) rather than issuing a
#   query op — R_USER_INVOKE (0x008) is not exercised and is not
#   declared.
# - KIND_TTY's R_TTY_WRITE (0x002) is the only right ls's tty_write
#   trampoline (src/tty_write.pdx) exercises; it is presently a plain
#   sys_write (sysno 1), with the real `cap_invoke(_ls_tty_slot,
#   TTY_OP_WRITE, ...)` wire deferred to R49.M1 per kind_tty.pdx §17.
#   The declared right is unchanged by that deferral — it is ls's
#   authored upper bound on TTY authority, not a statement that the
#   wire is live today.
# - KIND_PDXFS_FILE's R_PDXFS_FILE_READ (0x001 / PFF_OP_READ_BYTES)
#   is the only right declared: the readdir loop that will drive it is
#   still unwired (src/ls.pdx: "unused until readdir lands"). The
#   caps-decl-format.md §3.3 example for this exact tool declares the
#   identical mask. R_PDXFS_FILE_INVOKE (0x008), which `-l`'s
#   mode/len/mtime columns will eventually need for a direct per-field
#   query (src/long_format.pdx), is deliberately NOT reserved here —
#   unlike the volume trio's deferred-optional rights, this one has no
#   landed call site yet to point to; adding it is a follow-up decl
#   amendment once the readdir/query wiring lands, not a rights-narrow
#   of authority already declared.
# - The shell's exec-time cap_manifest_verify (libpdx-cap M2-001)
#   separately narrows the concrete KIND_PDXFS_FILE target to the
#   ls argument path (no ambient authority on the rest of the
#   filesystem) per r49-r50-plan.md §4.4. That per-argument narrowing
#   is a distinct mechanism from — and composes with — the kind+rights
#   narrow this file governs; this format has no path-template syntax
#   of its own.
# - KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT is optional and unbound: semantic_emit.pdx notes
#   the cap slot is populated by shell.M2 InitCap and consumed by
#   sys_ipc_send, but ls's default and `-l` render paths still write
#   through KIND_TTY only; --schema/--json compose their bytes and
#   also write through tty_write today. Declared early, per the M1-001
#   format doc's non-goals (§7), so the eventual wire bind is a
#   rights-narrow rather than a decl amendment.
#
# INVARIANT (v1.1.1 debugger finding 2, carried forward from the R50
# decl). The list below is the AUTHORITATIVE source for every declared
# semantic-pipe output schema ls emits on stdout. Two mirrors must stay
# in lock-step with it, or a `ls --schema` consumer preloads a decoder
# for a schema id no record ever arrives against:
#   1. src/schema_dump.pdx :: _sd_catalog_bytes -- one catalog line
#      per schema name below, LF-terminated. `_sd_catalog_len` is the
#      byte total.
#   2. src/semantic_emit.pdx :: _se_schema_name (and any future
#      per-schema name literal) -- one literal per schema declared
#      below. spipe_schema_id_from_name hashes over the bytes.
# Adding, removing, or renaming a schema is a three-file edit landing
# in one commit. tests/schema_dump_fixtures.pdx pins the catalog bytes
# byte-for-byte; a mismatch there is the tripwire.
#
# declares_output_schemas (kept as this comment block, not a decl-line
# — the strict line grammar above has no list syntax of its own; every
# `caps.decl :: declares_output_schemas` cross-reference in src/ and
# tests/ means this list):
#   - PdxFsDirEntry@0.1
#
# See also:
#   design/architecture/caps-decl-format.md  — format spec (paideia-os), §3.3 is this tool's own worked example
#   src/kernel/core/cap/reconcile.pdx        — kernel substrate (paideia-os)
#   design/tooling/r49-r50-plan.md §4.4/§5.4 — this tool's authoring wave (paideia-os)
